<!-- WHAT IS FINITO -->
<section id="what"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">The idea</span>
    <h2>A workflow is a set of states and the events that move between them</h2>
    <p class="lead">Finito models that directly. You define a <b>flow</b> of <b>states</b>; <b>events</b> trigger <b>transitions</b>, optionally running an action. Your entity carries its own state, and one call advances it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="card"><div class="ic">🟢</div><h3>States</h3><p><b>Manual states</b> wait for an event (a user or system action). <b>Auto states</b> decide their own next move by evaluating a condition on the data.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="ic">⚡</div><h3>Events &amp; transitions</h3><p>An <code>&lt;on&gt;</code> maps an <code>eventId</code> to a <code>newStateId</code> and an optional action component. That's the whole grammar of movement.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="ic">📦</div><h3>State entities</h3><p>Your domain object extends <code>StateEntity</code> and carries its current state. <code>STM.proceed(entity, event, payload)</code> runs the transition — actions, guards and all.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout key" style="margin-top:30px">
    <div class="t">One tiny interface at the core</div>
    <code>STM.proceed(entity, event, payload)</code> is the engine's whole runtime surface. Everything else — actions, entry/exit hooks, security, enablement, diagrams — hangs off the declarative flow definition.
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- HTML STATE-DIAGRAM SCHEMATIC -->
<section class="bg-soft" id="schematic"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">A flow, at a glance</span>
    <h2>A product-returns workflow</h2>
    <p class="lead">Here is the same state machine three ways — as a diagram, as the XML you write, and as the Mermaid &amp; PlantUML Finito generates from it. First, the diagram (rendered here in plain HTML).</p>
  </div>

  <div class="fsm">
    <div class="fsm-legend">
      <span><i class="dot start"></i> start</span>
      <span><i class="dot manual"></i> manual state</span>
      <span><i class="dot auto"></i> auto state (decides itself)</span>
      <span><i class="dot term"></i> terminal state</span>
    </div>
    <div class="track">
      <div class="node start" title="start"></div>
      <div class="arrow"><span class="line"></span></div>
      <div class="node"><span class="k">manual · initial</span>REQUESTED</div>
      <div class="arrow"><span class="lbl">approve</span><span class="line"></span></div>
      <div class="node"><span class="k">manual</span>APPROVED</div>
      <div class="arrow"><span class="lbl">ship</span><span class="line"></span></div>
      <div class="node"><span class="k">manual</span>LABEL_SENT</div>
      <div class="arrow"><span class="lbl">receive</span><span class="line"></span></div>
      <div class="node auto"><span class="k">auto · inspect</span>INSPECTION</div>
      <div class="branch">
        <div class="branch-row">
          <div class="arrow up"><span class="lbl">ok</span><span class="line"></span></div>
          <div class="node term"><span class="k">terminal</span>REFUNDED</div>
        </div>
        <div class="branch-row">
          <div class="arrow down"><span class="lbl">damaged</span><span class="line"></span></div>
          <div class="node term"><span class="k">terminal</span>REJECTED</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="fsm-cap">REQUESTED also transitions to REJECTED on <code>reject</code>. The <b>auto state</b> INSPECTION evaluates the item's condition and routes itself — no event needed from the caller.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- DSL -->
<section id="dsl"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">The DSL</span>
    <h2>You write the XML. That's the source of truth.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Declarative, reviewable, versionable. The same file drives the engine, the generated service, and every diagram.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="codewrap">
    <div class="bar"><i class="dotr"></i> returns-states.xml</div>
<pre><code><span class="tok-tag">&lt;states&gt;</span>
  <span class="tok-tag">&lt;flow</span> <span class="tok-attr">id</span>=<span class="tok-str">'returns-flow'</span> <span class="tok-attr">default</span>=<span class="tok-str">'true'</span><span class="tok-tag">&gt;</span>
    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;entry-action</span> <span class="tok-attr">componentName</span>=<span class="tok-str">"returnsEntryAction"</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>

    <span class="tok-cm">&lt;!-- manual state: waits for an event --&gt;</span>
    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;manual-state</span> <span class="tok-attr">id</span>=<span class="tok-str">'REQUESTED'</span> <span class="tok-attr">initialState</span>=<span class="tok-str">'true'</span> <span class="tok-attr">meta-mainPath</span>=<span class="tok-str">"true"</span><span class="tok-tag">&gt;</span>
      <span class="tok-tag">&lt;on</span> <span class="tok-attr">eventId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'approve'</span> <span class="tok-attr">newStateId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'APPROVED'</span> <span class="tok-attr">componentName</span>=<span class="tok-str">'ApproveReturn'</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>
      <span class="tok-tag">&lt;on</span> <span class="tok-attr">eventId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'reject'</span>  <span class="tok-attr">newStateId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'REJECTED'</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>
    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;/manual-state&gt;</span>

    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;manual-state</span> <span class="tok-attr">id</span>=<span class="tok-str">'APPROVED'</span> <span class="tok-attr">meta-mainPath</span>=<span class="tok-str">"true"</span><span class="tok-tag">&gt;</span>
      <span class="tok-tag">&lt;on</span> <span class="tok-attr">eventId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'ship'</span> <span class="tok-attr">newStateId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'LABEL_SENT'</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>
    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;/manual-state&gt;</span>

    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;manual-state</span> <span class="tok-attr">id</span>=<span class="tok-str">'LABEL_SENT'</span> <span class="tok-attr">meta-mainPath</span>=<span class="tok-str">"true"</span><span class="tok-tag">&gt;</span>
      <span class="tok-tag">&lt;on</span> <span class="tok-attr">eventId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'receive'</span> <span class="tok-attr">newStateId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'INSPECTION'</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>
    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;/manual-state&gt;</span>

    <span class="tok-cm">&lt;!-- auto state: decides its own next state from the data --&gt;</span>
    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;auto-state</span> <span class="tok-attr">id</span>=<span class="tok-str">'INSPECTION'</span> <span class="tok-attr">code</span>=<span class="tok-str">'payload.condition'</span><span class="tok-tag">&gt;</span>
      <span class="tok-tag">&lt;on</span> <span class="tok-attr">eventId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'ok'</span>      <span class="tok-attr">newStateId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'REFUNDED'</span> <span class="tok-attr">componentName</span>=<span class="tok-str">'IssueRefund'</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>
      <span class="tok-tag">&lt;on</span> <span class="tok-attr">eventId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'damaged'</span> <span class="tok-attr">newStateId</span>=<span class="tok-str">'REJECTED'</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>
    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;/auto-state&gt;</span>

    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;manual-state</span> <span class="tok-attr">id</span>=<span class="tok-str">'REFUNDED'</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>
    <span class="tok-tag">&lt;manual-state</span> <span class="tok-attr">id</span>=<span class="tok-str">'REJECTED'</span><span class="tok-tag">/&gt;</span>
  <span class="tok-tag">&lt;/flow&gt;</span>
<span class="tok-tag">&lt;/states&gt;</span></code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:26px">
    <div class="card"><div class="ic">🧩</div><h3>Actions on transitions</h3><p><code>componentName</code> runs code when an event fires. Add <code>entry-action</code> / <code>exit-action</code> per state, and a <code>default-transition-action</code> for the flow.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="ic">🔀</div><h3>Auto states &amp; guards</h3><p><code>&lt;auto-state code="…"&gt;</code> (and <code>&lt;if&gt;</code>) evaluate an OGNL expression on the entity to branch automatically — decisions live in the flow, not scattered in code.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="ic">🔐</div><h3>Policies in the flow</h3><p>Attach a <code>security-strategy</code> and <code>meta-acls</code> permissions to events, or an <code>enablement-strategy</code> to switch transitions on and off by configuration.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

